Create src/engine/MarkdownEngine.ts implementing the RenderEngine interface for markdown-to-HTML rendering.

First, ensure 'marked' library is installed:
npm install marked --prefix apps/flashcards/app

Implement:
```typescript
import { marked } from 'marked';
import type { RenderEngine } from '@/types';

const MarkdownEngine: RenderEngine = {
  render(data: any, target: HTMLElement): void {
    const markdown = String(data ?? '')
    target.innerHTML = marked.parse(markdown, { async: false }) as string
  }
}

export { MarkdownEngine }
```

Rules:
- render() is synchronous — uses marked.parse with async: false
- No precompute implementation — flip is always instant
- Engine must be pure — no side effects beyond target DOM
- Handle null/undefined data gracefully (render as empty string)

