Update src/screens/SessionScreen.tsx to implement the precompute lifecycle.

Add precompute support:
1. Import engineRegistry and normalizeCardSide from '@/engine/EngineRegistry'
2. Add state: const [precomputePromise, setPrecomputePromise] = useState<Promise<void> | null>(null)
3. After the question (front side) is displayed, start precompute for the back side:
   - Add a useEffect that triggers when currentCard changes and isFlipped is false
   - Resolve the back engine: const backEngine = engineRegistry.resolve(normalizeCardSide(currentCard.back).renderEngineId)
   - Call precompute if available: const promise = backEngine.precompute?.(normalizeCardSide(currentCard.back).data)
   - Store promise: setPrecomputePromise(promise ?? null)
4. Modify handleFlip to wait for precompute before flipping:
   ```typescript
   const handleFlip = useCallback(async () => {
     if (precomputePromise) {
       try {
         await precomputePromise
       } catch {
         // Fallback: proceed with flip even if precompute failed
       }
     }
     setIsFlipped((prev) => !prev)
   }, [precomputePromise])
   ```
5. Cancel/reset precompute when card changes (the useEffect on currentCard handles this)

Keep all existing functionality: shuffle, scoring, navigation, progress display.

CRITICAL: All existing tests in SessionScreen.test.tsx must pass without modification. TextEngine and MarkdownEngine do NOT implement precompute, so flip remains instant for current themes.

